  "final": "I fixed both files. `tsc -p tsconfig.json && node checks/public.cjs` passes. I didn't add new checks, so the retry, concurrency and conflict behaviour hasn't been tested beyond that one run.\n\n**`Ledger.apply` (`src/ledger.ts`)**\n- Receipts are now indexed by tenant, then key.\n- A repeat call with the same tenant, key and amount returns the original receipt object and adds no entry.\n- Reusing a tenant/key with a different amount throws `Error('key conflict')` and adds no entry.\n- The lookup and the insert happen in the same synchronous step, with no `await` between them. Concurrent calls with the same tenant and key therefore can't both debit.\n\n**`PaymentService.pay` (`src/service.ts`)**\n- Validation runs first, before any ledger or transport call. It requires a nonempty tenant and key, positive integer cents, and `attempts` as an integer from 1 to 5. Anything else throws `Error('invalid payment')`.\n- The debit is applied once, outside the retry loop.\n- Only `acknowledge` is retried, and always with that same receipt. It is retried only on `Transient`, up to `attempts` total tries.\n- If the tries run out, the last `Transient` is thrown unchanged. Any other error is thrown immediately without a retry.\n\nTwo concurrent `pay` calls with the same tenant, key and amount each get the same receipt, but each one calls `acknowledge` itself. I left it that way because the request only asked that the debit not be duplicated.",
